  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  messagePanel: {fileID: 15642466}
  bodyText: {fileID: 346420447}
  message: A galea was a Roman soldier's metal helmet, most famously worn by the
    heavy infantry of the legions. Some gladiators, specifically murmillo, also wore
    bronze galeae with face masks and decorations, often a fish on its crest.
