  message: A sarcophagus is a coffin, most commonly carved in stone, and usually
    displayed above ground, though it may also be buried. The earliest stone sarcophagi
    were used by Egyptian pharaohs of the 3rd dynasty, which reigned from about 2686
    to 2613 BC.
